# Release identity — copy to scripts/release.conf (gitignored) and fill in.
# Without this file, builds are ad-hoc signed and notarization is skipped:
# fine for local use, Gatekeeper will warn on other Macs.

# Developer ID Application certificate, exactly as `security find-identity -p
# codesigning -v` prints it:
#SIGNING_IDENTITY="Developer ID Application: Your Name (TEAMID1234)"

# Keychain profile for notarytool. One-time setup:
#   xcrun notarytool store-credentials banshee-notarize \
#       --apple-id <apple-id> --team-id <team-id>
#NOTARIZE_PROFILE="banshee-notarize"

# BUILD SERVER shape (a headless build machine): an App Store Connect API key instead
# of the keychain profile — a file, works headless from launchd/ssh. When these
# three are set they take precedence over NOTARIZE_PROFILE; setting only some of
# them is a hard error, not a fall-through.
#NOTARY_KEY_PATH="$HOME/.config/banshee-build/AuthKey.p8"
#NOTARY_KEY_ID="XXXXXXXXXX"
#NOTARY_ISSUER_ID="11111111-2222-3333-4444-555555555555"
# The keychain FILE holding the Developer ID, for a machine where it is not in the
# login keychain (codesign --keychain). Unlock it first (`security unlock-keychain`).
#SIGNING_KEYCHAIN="$HOME/Library/Keychains/banshee-build.keychain-db"
# The Sparkle EdDSA PRIVATE key as a file (generate_keys -x), for a machine whose
# keychain does not hold it. Same key as everywhere else — never regenerate.
#SPARKLE_PRIVATE_KEY_FILE="$HOME/.config/banshee-build/sparkle_private_key"
# This file's location is overridable: BANSHEE_RELEASE_CONF=/path/to/release.conf.

# Optional self-healing: when the keychain profile becomes inaccessible
# (data-protection keychain locks after sleep/iCloud events), build-dmg.sh
# re-provisions it if APPLE_ID and APPLE_TEAM_ID are exported — notarytool
# prompts for the app-specific password interactively (never on the command
# line, where `ps` could expose it).

# Sparkle auto-update. The PUBLIC EdDSA key (the private key stays in the
# keychain via Sparkle's generate_keys). build-dmg.sh REFUSES a real-identity
# build without this (SKIP_SPARKLE=1 overrides) — a signed DMG that cannot
# auto-update must be a deliberate act, never an accident.
#SPARKLE_PUBLIC_KEY=""
# Where publish.sh uploads the DMG + appcast. Normally UNSET: releases live on the
# source repository itself (GITHUB_REPOSITORY on the runner, `origin` on a developer
# machine). Set this only to publish somewhere else.
#RELEASES_REPO="youruser/some-other-repo"
